The quorum of the general assembly is one third of the members present, as established by the amendment adopted 2 May 2026. [[cite:obs-d0086e18845573f97c098e9c7e8d509c697a2f79 "Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present."]]

Where the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies. [[cite:obs-d0086e18845573f97c098e9c7e8d509c697a2f79 "Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present."]]

The bylaws state that the general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present, but this is superseded by the amendment. [[cite:obs-866f485db2e1ab744efb94a837890dc74426b27a "The general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present."]]